From 5dbc491f4222331dca936fb03fbaf36f0a2a25c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Beckett <bob.beckett@collabora.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 13:46:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 150/188] cfg80211: add 6 GHz passive-scan rule to the world
 regulatory domain
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The built-in world domain ("00") has no 6 GHz frequency rules, causing
every 6 GHz channel to be marked IEEE80211_CHAN_DISABLED.  Disabled
channels are silently dropped from scan requests in nl80211, so drivers
never receive them, no beacons are ever heard, and 6 GHz-only networks
are completely invisible regardless of hardware capability.

Add a single NO_IR rule covering the full 6 GHz WiFi band
(UNII-5 through UNII-8, 5945–7125 MHz).  This is consistent with the
treatment of every 5 GHz channel in the world domain, all of which carry
NO_IR rather than being disabled outright.

With NO_IR instead of DISABLED:
  - scan requests include 6 GHz channels in passive (listen-only) mode;
  - when a beacon is received, regulatory_hint_found_beacon() enqueues a
    beacon hint, handle_reg_beacon() clears NO_IR for that channel, and
    NL80211_CMD_REG_BEACON_HINT is delivered to user space;
  - wpa_supplicant / iwd can then associate normally.

This activates the existing beacon-hint path for 6 GHz and requires no
driver changes.  Drivers that already manage their own regulatory domain
(REGULATORY_WIPHY_SELF_MANAGED) are unaffected.

Assisted-by: Claude:Sonnet 4.6
Signed-off-by: Robert Beckett <bob.beckett@collabora.com>
---
 net/wireless/reg.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/wireless/reg.c b/net/wireless/reg.c
index 1e8214d6b..0e13e4511 100644
--- a/net/wireless/reg.c
+++ b/net/wireless/reg.c
@@ -231,7 +231,7 @@ static DECLARE_WORK(reg_work, reg_todo);
 
 /* We keep a static world regulatory domain in case of the absence of CRDA */
 static const struct ieee80211_regdomain world_regdom = {
-	.n_reg_rules = 8,
+	.n_reg_rules = 9,
 	.alpha2 =  "00",
 	.reg_rules = {
 		/* IEEE 802.11b/g, channels 1..11 */
@@ -264,6 +264,17 @@ static const struct ieee80211_regdomain world_regdom = {
 		REG_RULE(5745-10, 5825+10, 80, 6, 20,
 			NL80211_RRF_NO_IR),
 
+		/* IEEE 802.11ax/WiFi 6E, 6 GHz (UNII-5 through UNII-8,
+		 * channels 1..233).  Allow passive scanning so that beacon
+		 * hints can unlock individual channels once an AP is observed
+		 * transmitting there.  This mirrors the treatment of 5 GHz
+		 * channels in this world domain and enables connection to
+		 * 6 GHz-only networks without requiring the user to first set
+		 * a country code.
+		 */
+		REG_RULE(5955-10, 7125+10, 320, 0, 23,
+			NL80211_RRF_NO_IR),
+
 		/* IEEE 802.11ad (60GHz), channels 1..3 */
 		REG_RULE(56160+2160*1-1080, 56160+2160*3+1080, 2160, 0, 0, 0),
 	}
-- 
